#conversation file
version=0.1

question "Is here alright? By the lamp?" {
    tag=Room_01
    answer=Here's fine. Everywhere's fine.
    answer=Sorry, the place is a state. I didn't know if you'd actually come.

    question "Why wouldn't I?" {
        tag=Room_01
        answer=People say things.
        answer=Anyway. You're here. Hi.

        question "Introduce yourself?" {
            tag=Room_01
            answer=Thiago. Twenty-four.
            answer=Two years on T. Which is going great except for this.

            question "Except for what?" {
                tag=Room_01
                answer=The hair. Look at it.
                answer=Nobody tells you that bit. They tell you the voice and the shoulders and the good stuff.
                answer=Nobody sits you down and says, by the way, you'll get exactly what you asked for and then start losing your hair like your uncle.

                question "Alright. Questions." {
                    id=shared1
                    tag=Room_01
                    answer=Okay. Be gentle, I'm delicate.

                    question "Are you?" {
                        tag=Room_01
                        answer=No.
                        answer=I'm strong, Ill figure it out…but i always cry first.
                        answer=That's the actual order. Every time. Cry, then figure it out. Never once been able to swap them round.
                    }

                    question "Tell me about your arms." {
                        tag=Room_02
                        answer=Arms, yeah.
                        answer=Do you ever catch yourself pushing your finger into a bruise. Because even though it hurts the pain sends feedback, the pain is information.

                        question "Information about what?" {
                            tag=Room_02
                            answer=That there's something there. That you're not making it up.
                            answer=Half of this is being told you're making it up. By doctors, by family, by yourself mostly.
                            answer=You press it and it answers back. Nothing else answers back.

                            question "Nothing?" {
                                tag=Room_02
                                loop_to=shared1
                                answer=All the feelings you suppress turn into illness.
                                answer=I've been suppressing since I was about eleven, so you can do the maths on that.
                            }
                        }
                    }

                    question "You said people say things. About you." {
                        tag=Room_02
                        answer=Not about me exactly. About people like me.
                        answer=I don't read it any more. I did for about a year and it was like drinking from a tap you know is bad.

                        question "Does it get to you?" {
                            tag=Room_02
                            answer=Everytime i trusted someone i ended up hurt, so finally i stopped trusting everybody. I would never be hurt again.

                            question "How's that working out?" {
                                tag=Room_02
                                answer=...
                                answer=Ha.
                                answer=Yeah. Fair.
                                answer=Turns out you can't switch it off in one direction only. You go quiet with everyone.

                                question "Even the good ones?" {
                                    tag=Room_03
                                    loop_to=shared1
                                    answer=Especially the good ones. They're the ones that can actually do damage.
                                    answer=You can be perfectly safe and completely alone and those are not two separate things, they're the same thing wearing different coats.
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }

                    question "Is there someone special in your life?" {
                        tag=Room_03
                        answer=...
                        answer=How did you—
                        answer=Right. The phone's face-down. That's a tell, is it.

                        question "It's face-down and you've looked at it four times." {
                            tag=Room_03
                            answer=Five.
                            answer=Seven months. Ended in March.
                            answer=He isnt going to call, I should get stoned and go to bed.

                            question "Is that tonight's plan?" {
                                tag=Room_03
                                answer=That's every night's plan. That's the whole plan.
                                answer=I say it out loud like it's a decision. It's not a decision, it's a weather report.

                                question "Do you want him to call?" {
                                    tag=Room_03
                                    answer=No.
                                    answer=...
                                    answer=Yes. Obviously yes.
                                    answer=He was kind to me for a bit and I hadn't had that and I don't think I knew what it was going to do to me when it stopped.

                                    question "What did it do?" {
                                        tag=Room_04
                                        loop_to=shared1
                                        answer=Made everything before it look worse.
                                        answer=That's the thing nobody warns you about kindness. It shows you the size of the room you'd been living in.
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }

                    question "Tell me about the pills." {
                        tag=Room_04
                        answer=...
                        answer=Okay.
                        answer=Two years ago. I'm not going to do the details, is that alright.

                        question "That's alright." {
                            tag=Room_04
                            answer=Thanks.
                            answer=I can't help but remember the state nobody found me in.

                            question "Say that again?" {
                                tag=Room_04
                                answer=Nobody found me.
                                answer=That's the bit. I woke up. On my own. Sunday afternoon, sun coming through, and the flat exactly how I'd left it.
                                answer=I'd sort of assumed there'd be someone. Not rescue, I don't mean rescue. Just — someone.

                                question "What did you do?" {
                                    tag=Room_04
                                    answer=I cleaned up.
                                    answer=I got a bin bag and I cleaned up and I went to work on the Monday.
                                    answer=Nobody has ever known about it except a nurse I saw once and now you.

                                    question "Why tell me?" {
                                        tag=Room_05
                                        answer=Why do people want me to clear my mind out, why do you want to forget about it, you can't just ignore everything like you gotta figure some shit out.
                                        answer=Everyone in my life wants me over it. My mum says move on like it's a bus.
                                        answer=You're the first person who's sat down and asked me to go back into it on purpose.

                                        question "Does that help?" {
                                            tag=Room_05
                                            loop_to=shared1
                                            answer=I don't know yet.
                                            answer=Ask me in a week.
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }

                    question "Do you think you're a good person?" {
                        tag=Room_05
                        answer=No.
                        answer=I speak about kindess but I've hurt people.

                        question "Who?" {
                            tag=Room_05
                            answer=My sister, mostly. My mum.
                            answer=Not on purpose. That's almost worse. I wasn't cruel, I was just gone for about three years.
                            answer=You can do a lot of damage by being absent. Nobody counts that as damage.

                            question "Have you told them?" {
                                tag=Room_05
                                loop_to=shared1
                                answer=No.
                                answer=You'd have to explain where you were, and I don't know where I was.
                            }
                        }
                    }

                    question "That's all I wanted to ask." {
                        tag=Room_05
                        answer=Oh.
                        answer=Right, no, that's — that's fine.

                        question "Are you okay?" {
                            tag=Room_05
                            answer=All this has been pretty overwhelming, you know; I don't get out much and i thnk i really needed this, so thank you, i had a really good time.

                            question "..." {
                                tag=Room_05
                                ending
                                ending_text=They said they had a good time. They meant it, entirely, and that is the saddest sentence anyone says in this project.
                                ending_text=The phone did not light up once in the whole hour.
                                ending_text=They will get stoned and go to bed, exactly as forecast, and tomorrow will be a Tuesday.
                                answer=Sorry. That's a weird thing to say about this.
                                answer=I can come back if you want. I mean — if you need more. For the film.
                                answer=...
